tctiSH's changes to QEMU, against utmapp/qemu v10.0.12-utm.

Generated with, from a checkout of that tag:

    git diff v10.0.12-utm -- <the files below>

What is in here, roughly in order of size:

  tcg/region.c              the StikJIT blessing protocol, and code cache
                            ballooning -- grow/shrink/release plus the
                            tctish_* accessors the app reads through dlsym;
                            and releasing all of it while the VM is parked
  hw/9pfs/*                 snapshot support: the migration blocker removed,
                            and in-flight virtqueue elements saved/restored;
                            and 9p-util.h, which lets the server follow a
                            symlink out of the export -- the thing the iOS
                            folder mounts are built on
  system/vl.c               a named snapshot that is absent is a cold boot
                            rather than a fatal error
  system/physmem.c          discard guest RAM by mapping fresh memory over it,
                            since Darwin's MADV_DONTNEED frees nothing -- this
                            is what makes free page reporting return memory
  migration/ram.c           don't read guest pages the kernel has no copy of
                            when saving or loading a snapshot; on Darwin each
                            read would charge a page, so either took the
                            footprint to the whole of guest RAM. And hand back
                            the resident zero pages a stopped save finds
  migration/*-hmp-cmds.c,   `park` and `unpark`: give a stopped, saved VM's RAM
  hmp-commands.hx,          back while the app is in the background, and load
  include/monitor/hmp.h     it back in the same process on return
  system/cpu-timers.c       catch the VM's clock up whenever it starts after a
                            stop or a snapshot load, as if it had only been
                            suspended: saves, parking, and resuming after a
                            kill no longer leave the guest's time behind
  system/runstate.c,        a parked VM refuses `cont` and `savevm` until a
  monitor/qmp-cmds.c,       load or a reset makes its RAM whole again
  migration/savevm.c
  include/system/*.h        declarations for the above
  system/qemu.symbols       export the tctish_* accessors; the shared-library
                            build hides anything not listed here
  accel/tcg/tb-maint.c      release the unused tail of the code buffer at a
                            tb flush, and the bottom half that asks for one
  accel/tcg/tcg-all.c       create that bottom half at init
  include/tcg/tcg.h         declarations for the above
  configure                 tell meson it cannot run iOS binaries; host_os is
                            "darwin" for macOS and iOS alike
  meson.build               order the emulator's compile after qapi generation
  subprojects/slirp.wrap    fix the [provide] variable name; libslirp renamed
                            it in 4.9.0 and this fork's revision bump missed it

The last two are upstream bugs rather than tctiSH features, and are worth
sending to UTM rather than carrying for ever.
